# Diagnosis

Two independent defects, plus a third one hiding behind them (state-destroying re-index).

## Root cause A — the "circular dependency"

The comment in the seed is a red herring:

```hcl
# Circular dependency: this output references the instance before it exists in plan
output "db_endpoint" {
  value = aws_db_instance.main[0].endpoint
}
```

HCL is declarative. Declaration order is irrelevant, and an `output` is always a **leaf** node in the dependency graph — it can never participate in a cycle. That output is not your problem.

`Error: Cycle:` in this spine comes from one of two real patterns, both of which appear as soon as you flesh out the scenario:

**A1 — inline security group rules that cross-reference.** Terraform tracks dependencies at *resource* granularity, not attribute granularity. Two SGs that reference each other inline is a genuine cycle:

```hcl
# ✗ Cycle: aws_security_group.db → aws_security_group.nodes → aws_security_group.db
resource "aws_security_group" "db" {
  ingress { from_port = 5432 to_port = 5432 protocol = "tcp"
            security_groups = [aws_security_group.nodes.id] }
}
resource "aws_security_group" "nodes" {
  egress  { from_port = 5432 to_port = 5432 protocol = "tcp"
            security_groups = [aws_security_group.db.id] }
}
```

**Fix:** hoist rules into standalone resources so the rule becomes a third graph node depending on both SGs:

```hcl
resource "aws_security_group" "db"    { vpc_id = var.vpc_id }
resource "aws_security_group" "nodes" { vpc_id = var.vpc_id }

resource "aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule" "db_from_nodes" {
  security_group_id            = aws_security_group.db.id
  referenced_security_group_id = aws_security_group.nodes.id
  from_port = 5432
  to_port   = 5432
  ip_protocol = "tcp"
}
```

**A2 — secret ↔ database.** The connection-string secret needs `aws_db_instance.main.endpoint`; people then reference `aws_secretsmanager_secret.db.arn` back into the DB (in `tags`, or `master_user_secret_kms_key_id`). Cycle.

**Fix:** keep the flow strictly one-directional: `secret (container, no value)` → `db_instance` → `secret_version (holds endpoint)`. Never read the secret back into the DB.

## Root cause B — `count` vs `for_each`

```hcl
resource "aws_db_instance" "main" {
  identifier = "${var.env}-db"   # ← singular string
  count      = length(var.envs)  # ← plural list
}
```

`var.env` (string) and `var.envs` (list) are two different mental models fighting in one resource. Symptoms you'll hit, in order:

| Symptom | Cause |
|---|---|
| `Because aws_db_instance.main has "count" set, its attributes must be accessed on specific instances` | any reference without `[idx]` |
| `Invalid index: The given key does not identify an element in this collection value` | switching to `for_each` while consumers still index `[0]` |
| `The "count" value depends on resource attributes that cannot be determined until apply` | `var.envs` sourced from a data source / another resource |
| **silent DB destroy + recreate** | `envs = ["dev","prod"]` → remove `"dev"` → `main[1]` re-indexes to `main[0]`; prod's database is destroyed |

Also note every instance gets `identifier = "${var.env}-db"` — the *same* name for all N instances. `terraform apply` with `envs = ["dev","prod"]` fails with `DBInstanceAlreadyExists`.

**The rule:**

- `count` → boolean toggle only (`count = var.enable_x ? 1 : 0`)
- `for_each` → a set/map of *stably named* peers within one environment
- **neither** → environments. Environments are separate root modules and separate state files. That is the only way to satisfy acceptance criterion 7.

---

# Minimal patch (if you just want it to apply)

```hcl
resource "aws_db_instance" "main" {
  identifier        = "${var.env}-db"
  allocated_storage = 20
  engine            = "postgres"
  engine_version    = "16.1"
  instance_class    = var.instance_class

  db_name  = var.db_name
  username = var.db_user
  password = var.db_password

  # count removed — one DB per env, one env per state
  multi_az                = var.multi_az
  storage_encrypted       = true
  publicly_accessible     = false
  backup_retention_period = 14
  deletion_protection     = true
  skip_final_snapshot     = false
  final_snapshot_identifier = "${var.env}-db-final-${formatdate("YYYYMMDDhhmmss", timestamp())}"
}

output "db_endpoint" {
  value = aws_db_instance.main.endpoint   # no index
}
```

**Do not apply this without a `moved` block** — dropping `count` changes the resource address from `aws_db_instance.main[0]` to `aws_db_instance.main`, and Terraform will read that as destroy + create:

```hcl
moved {
  from = aws_db_instance.main[0]
  to   = aws_db_instance.main
}
```

Delete `variable "envs"` entirely.

---

# The idiomatic rebuild

## Layout

```
.
├── modules/
│   ├── network/       # VPC, subnets, NAT, EKS subnet tags
│   ├── cluster/       # EKS + managed node group + IRSA OIDC provider
│   ├── data/          # RDS + SGs + Secrets Manager
│   ├── storage/       # S3 + versioning/SSE/PAB + optional CRR
│   ├── identity/      # dev: IAM user | prod: IRSA role
│   └── edge/          # ALB :443 + ACM, optional CloudFront
└── envs/
    ├── dev/{main.tf,backend.tf,dev.tfvars,secrets.dev.enc.yaml}
    └── prod/{main.tf,backend.tf,prod.tfvars,secrets.prod.enc.yaml}
```

Separate root dirs + separate backend keys → prod plan physically cannot touch dev state.

## `modules/data/main.tf` — cycle-free RDS + secret

```hcl
resource "aws_db_subnet_group" "this" {
  name       = "${var.env}-db"
  subnet_ids = var.private_subnet_ids
}

resource "aws_security_group" "db" {
  name   = "${var.env}-db"
  vpc_id = var.vpc_id
}

# standalone rule → breaks the SG↔SG cycle
resource "aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule" "from_nodes" {
  security_group_id            = aws_security_group.db.id
  referenced_security_group_id = var.node_security_group_id
  from_port                    = 5432
  to_port                      = 5432
  ip_protocol                  = "tcp"
  description                  = "postgres from eks nodes"
}

resource "aws_kms_key" "db" {
  count                   = var.encrypt_with_cmk ? 1 : 0   # ← legitimate count
  description             = "${var.env} rds cmk"
  enable_key_rotation     = true
  deletion_window_in_days = 30
}

resource "aws_db_instance" "this" {
  identifier     = "${var.env}-db"
  engine         = "postgres"
  engine_version = "16.1"
  instance_class = var.instance_class

  allocated_storage     = var.allocated_storage
  max_allocated_storage = var.allocated_storage * 4

  db_name  = var.db_name
  username = var.db_user
  password = var.db_password

  db_subnet_group_name   = aws_db_subnet_group.this.name
  vpc_security_group_ids = [aws_security_group.db.id]

  multi_az            = var.multi_az
  publicly_accessible = false                              # AC 2
  storage_encrypted   = true                               # AC 2
  kms_key_id          = try(aws_kms_key.db[0].arn, null)

  backup_retention_period    = var.backup_retention_days   # AC 2 (>= 7)
  backup_window              = "03:00-04:00"
  auto_minor_version_upgrade = true
  deletion_protection        = var.deletion_protection     # AC 2
  skip_final_snapshot        = false
  final_snapshot_identifier  = "${var.env}-db-final"
  copy_tags_to_snapshot      = true

  performance_insights_enabled = var.multi_az
  enabled_cloudwatch_logs_exports = ["postgresql", "upgrade"]

  lifecycle {
    ignore_changes = [password]   # rotated out-of-band
  }
}

# ── one-directional: secret container → db → secret version ──────────
resource "aws_secretsmanager_secret" "db_url" {
  name                    = "${var.env}/app/db-url"
  kms_key_id              = try(aws_kms_key.db[0].arn, null)
  recovery_window_in_days = var.env == "prod" ? 30 : 7
}

resource "aws_secretsmanager_secret_version" "db_url" {
  secret_id = aws_secretsmanager_secret.db_url.id
  secret_string = jsonencode({
    host     = aws_db_instance.this.address
    port     = aws_db_instance.this.port
    dbname   = aws_db_instance.this.db_name
    username = aws_db_instance.this.username
    password = var.db_password
    url      = "postgresql://${var.db_user}:${var.db_password}@${aws_db_instance.this.endpoint}/${var.db_name}?sslmode=require"
  })
}
```

`terraform graph` for this is a DAG: `secret → version ← db → sg ← rule → node_sg`. No back-edges.

## `modules/storage/main.tf` — S3 + conditional CRR

```hcl
terraform {
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source                = "hashicorp/aws"
      version               = "~> 5.0"
      configuration_aliases = [aws.replica]
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "assets" { bucket = var.bucket_name }

resource "aws_s3_bucket_versioning" "assets" {            # AC 1
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  versioning_configuration { status = "Enabled" }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration" "assets" {  # AC 1
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  rule {
    apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {
      sse_algorithm     = var.kms_key_arn == null ? "AES256" : "aws:kms"
      kms_master_key_id = var.kms_key_arn
    }
    bucket_key_enabled = true
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block" "assets" {   # AC 1
  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  block_public_acls       = true
  block_public_policy     = true
  ignore_public_acls      = true
  restrict_public_buckets = true
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls" "assets" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  rule { object_ownership = "BucketOwnerEnforced" }
}

# ── cross-region replication: prod only, toggled with count ──────────
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "replica" {
  count    = var.enable_replication ? 1 : 0
  provider = aws.replica
  bucket   = "${var.bucket_name}-replica"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_versioning" "replica" {
  count    = var.enable_replication ? 1 : 0
  provider = aws.replica
  bucket   = aws_s3_bucket.replica[0].id
  versioning_configuration { status = "Enabled" }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "replication" {
  count = var.enable_replication ? 1 : 0
  name  = "${var.bucket_name}-replication"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{ Effect = "Allow", Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
                   Principal = { Service = "s3.amazonaws.com" } }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "replication" {
  count = var.enable_replication ? 1 : 0
  role  = aws_iam_role.replication[0].id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      { Effect = "Allow",
        Action = ["s3:GetReplicationConfiguration", "s3:ListBucket"],
        Resource = [aws_s3_bucket.assets.arn] },
      { Effect = "Allow",
        Action = ["s3:GetObjectVersionForReplication", "s3:GetObjectVersionAcl",
                  "s3:GetObjectVersionTagging"],
        Resource = ["${aws_s3_bucket.assets.arn}/*"] },
      { Effect = "Allow",
        Action = ["s3:ReplicateObject", "s3:ReplicateDelete", "s3:ReplicateTags"],
        Resource = ["${aws_s3_bucket.replica[0].arn}/*"] },
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_replication_configuration" "assets" {
  count      = var.enable_replication ? 1 : 0
  bucket     = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  role       = aws_iam_role.replication[0].arn
  depends_on = [aws_s3_bucket_versioning.assets, aws_s3_bucket_versioning.replica]

  rule {
    id       = "assets-to-usw2"
    status   = "Enabled"
    priority = 0
    filter {}
    delete_marker_replication { status = "Enabled" }
    destination {
      bucket        = aws_s3_bucket.replica[0].arn
      storage_class = "STANDARD_IA"
    }
  }
}
```

Dev passes `providers = { aws = aws, aws.replica = aws }` and `enable_replication = false`, so nothing extra is created.

## `modules/cluster/main.tf` — EKS

```hcl
resource "aws_iam_role" "cluster" {
  name = "${var.name}-cluster"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version   = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{ Effect = "Allow", Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
                   Principal = { Service = "eks.amazonaws.com" } }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "cluster" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.cluster.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSClusterPolicy"
}

resource "aws_eks_cluster" "this" {
  name     = var.name
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.cluster.arn
  version  = var.kubernetes_version

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids              = var.private_subnet_ids
    endpoint_private_access = true
    endpoint_public_access  = var.env != "prod"
  }

  access_config { authentication_mode = "API" }
  depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.cluster]
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "node" {
  name = "${var.name}-node"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version   = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{ Effect = "Allow", Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
                   Principal = { Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com" } }]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "node" {
  # for_each over a static set of peers — the correct use of for_each
  for_each = toset([
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy",
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy",
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly",
  ])
  role       = aws_iam_role.node.name
  policy_arn = each.value
}

resource "aws_eks_node_group" "this" {                    # AC 5
  cluster_name    = aws_eks_cluster.this.name
  node_group_name = "${var.name}-default"
  node_role_arn   = aws_iam_role.node.arn
  subnet_ids      = var.private_subnet_ids
  instance_types  = [var.instance_type]                   # t3.medium | t3.large

  scaling_config {
    desired_size = var.node_count                         # 2 | 4
    min_size     = var.node_count
    max_size     = var.node_count * 2
  }
  update_config { max_unavailable = 1 }
  depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.node]
}

data "tls_certificate" "oidc" {
  url = aws_eks_cluster.this.identity[0].oidc[0].issuer
}

resource "aws_iam_openid_connect_provider" "this" {
  url             = aws_eks_cluster.this.identity[0].oidc[0].issuer
  client_id_list  = ["sts.amazonaws.com"]
  thumbprint_list = [data.tls_certificate.oidc.certificates[0].sha1_fingerprint]
}
```

## `modules/identity/main.tf` — least privilege, env-shaped

```hcl
data "aws_iam_policy_document" "app" {
  statement {
    sid       = "AssetsObjectRW"
    actions   = ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject", "s3:DeleteObject"]   # AC 4: no s3:*
    resources = ["${var.assets_bucket_arn}/*"]
  }
  statement {
    sid       = "AssetsList"
    actions   = ["s3:ListBucket"]
    resources = [var.assets_bucket_arn]
  }
  statement {
    sid       = "ReadDbSecret"
    actions   = ["secretsmanager:GetSecretValue"]
    resources = [var.db_secret_arn]
  }
}

# ── dev: programmatic user ───────────────────────────────────────────
resource "aws_iam_user" "app" {
  count = var.mode == "user" ? 1 : 0
  name  = "${var.env}-app"
}

resource "aws_iam_user_policy" "app" {
  count  = var.mode == "user" ? 1 : 0
  user   = aws_iam_user.app[0].name
  policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.app.json
}

resource "aws_iam_access_key" "app" {
  count = var.mode == "user" ? 1 : 0
  user  = aws_iam_user.app[0].name
}

# ── prod: OIDC / IRSA role, no long-lived credentials ────────────────
data "aws_iam_policy_document" "trust" {
  count = var.mode == "oidc" ? 1 : 0
  statement {
    effect  = "Allow"
    actions = ["sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity"]
    principals {
      type        = "Federated"
      identifiers = [var.oidc_provider_arn]
    }
    condition {
      test     = "StringEquals"
      variable = "${var.oidc_provider_url}:sub"
      values   = ["system:serviceaccount:${var.namespace}:${var.service_account}"]
    }
    condition {
      test     = "StringEquals"
      variable = "${var.oidc_provider_url}:aud"
      values   = ["sts.amazonaws.com"]
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "app" {
  count                = var.mode == "oidc" ? 1 : 0
  name                 = "${var.env}-app"
  assume_role_policy   = data.aws_iam_policy_document.trust[0].json
  max_session_duration = 3600
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "app" {
  count  = var.mode == "oidc" ? 1 : 0
  role   = aws_iam_role.app[0].id
  policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.app.json
}
```

## `modules/edge/main.tf` — HTTPS

```hcl
resource "aws_lb" "this" {
  name               = "${var.env}-app"
  internal           = var.internal          # dev: true
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  subnets            = var.internal ? var.private_subnet_ids : var.public_subnet_ids
  security_groups    = [aws_security_group.alb.id]
  drop_invalid_header_fields = true
}

resource "aws_lb_target_group" "this" {
  name        = "${var.env}-app"
  port        = 8080
  protocol    = "HTTP"
  target_type = "ip"
  vpc_id      = var.vpc_id
  health_check { path = "/healthz" matcher = "200" }
}

# AC 6: 443 only. No :80 listener, therefore no forced 80->443 redirect.
resource "aws_lb_listener" "https" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.this.arn
  port              = 443
  protocol          = "HTTPS"
  ssl_policy        = "ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06"
  certificate_arn   = var.acm_certificate_arn
  default_action { type = "forward" target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.this.arn }
}

# ── prod only ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
resource "aws_cloudfront_distribution" "this" {
  count   = var.enable_cloudfront ? 1 : 0
  enabled = true
  aliases = var.domain_names

  origin {
    domain_name = aws_lb.this.dns_name
    origin_id   = "alb"
    custom_origin_config {
      http_port              = 80
      https_port             = 443
      origin_protocol_policy = "https-only"
      origin_ssl_protocols   = ["TLSv1.2"]
    }
  }

  default_cache_behavior {
    target_origin_id       = "alb"
    viewer_protocol_policy = "redirect-to-https"
    allowed_methods        = ["GET", "HEAD", "OPTIONS", "PUT", "POST", "PATCH", "DELETE"]
    cached_methods         = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    cache_policy_id        = data.aws_cloudfront_cache_policy.disabled.id
  }

  viewer_certificate {
    acm_certificate_arn      = var.cloudfront_certificate_arn  # must be us-east-1
    ssl_support_method       = "sni-only"
    minimum_protocol_version = "TLSv1.2_2021"
  }

  restrictions { geo_restriction { restriction_type = "none" } }
}
```

## `envs/prod/main.tf`

```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = "~> 1.9"
  required_providers {
    aws  = { source = "hashicorp/aws",  version = "~> 5.0" }
    sops = { source = "carlpett/sops",  version = "~> 1.0" }
    tls  = { source = "hashicorp/tls",  version = "~> 4.0" }
  }
}

provider "aws" { region = var.region }                    # us-east-1
provider "aws" { alias = "replica"  region = "us-west-2" }
provider "aws" { alias = "us_east_1" region = "us-east-1" }  # CloudFront ACM

# AC 3: ciphertext in git, decrypted in-memory at plan time via KMS
data "sops_file" "secrets" { source_file = "secrets.prod.enc.yaml" }

module "network" {
  source = "../../modules/network"
  env    = "prod"
  cidr   = "10.20.0.0/16"
}

module "cluster" {
  source             = "../../modules/cluster"
  env                = "prod"
  name               = "prod-app"
  kubernetes_version = "1.30"
  private_subnet_ids = module.network.private_subnet_ids
  instance_type      = "t3.large"     # AC 5
  node_count         = 4              # AC 5
}

module "storage" {
  source             = "../../modules/storage"
  providers          = { aws = aws, aws.replica = aws.replica }
  bucket_name        = "acme-prod-assets"
  kms_key_arn        = aws_kms_key.assets.arn
  enable_replication = true           # AC 1 + prod CRR to us-west-2
}

module "data" {
  source                 = "../../modules/data"
  env                    = "prod"
  vpc_id                 = module.network.vpc_id
  private_subnet_ids     = module.network.private_subnet_ids
  node_security_group_id = module.cluster.node_security_group_id
  instance_class         = "db.t3.medium"
  multi_az               = true       # AC 2
  encrypt_with_cmk       = true
  backup_retention_days  = 30         # AC 2 (>= 7)
  deletion_protection    = true       # AC 2
  db_password            = data.sops_file.secrets.data["db_password"]
}

module "identity" {
  source            = "../../modules/identity"
  env               = "prod"
  mode              = "oidc"          # AC 4
  oidc_provider_arn = module.cluster.oidc_provider_arn
  oidc_provider_url = module.cluster.oidc_provider_url
  namespace         = "app"
  service_account   = "web"
  assets_bucket_arn = module.storage.bucket_arn
  db_secret_arn     = module.data.secret_arn
}

module "edge" {
  source                     = "../../modules/edge"
  env                        = "prod"
  vpc_id                     = module.network.vpc_id
  public_subnet_ids          = module.network.public_subnet_ids
  internal                   = false
  acm_certificate_arn        = aws_acm_certificate.regional.arn
  enable_cloudfront          = true   # AC 6
  cloudfront_certificate_arn = aws_acm_certificate.edge.arn
  domain_names               = ["app.example.com"]
}
```

`envs/dev/main.tf` is the same shape with `mode = "user"`, `instance_type = "t3.medium"`, `node_count = 2`, `multi_az = false`, `enable_replication = false`, `internal = true`, `enable_cloudfront = false`.

## `envs/prod/backend.tf` — is
